        "original_id": "d4bec15c-8e7d-5b55-b924-428507bfb6b5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Independent Commission on the Voting System, Jenkins Commission\n- People: Roy Jenkins\n- Places: United Kingdom\n- Topics: electoral system reform, British politics\n\nFacts:\n- Roy Harris Jenkins, Baron Jenkins of Hillhead, was born on 11 November 1920 and died on 5 January 2003.\n- Roy Jenkins was a British politician associated with the Labour Party, SDP, and Liberal Democrat parties, and he was also a biographer of British political leaders.\n- The Independent Commission on the Voting System was popularly known as the Jenkins Commission because Roy Jenkins served as its chairman.\n- The Independent Commission on the Voting System was a commission that examined possible reform of the United Kingdom electoral system.",
